,"expedition","tropical","wildlife"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"primary","diveglobal":"destination","expedition":"evidenced","ocean":"destination","romance":"destination","tropical":"evidenced","wildlife":"evidenced"},"commission_lane":["operator","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane","si_basis":"the dossier''s own SI block filed this jewel under a heading resolving to ''wildlife'' via ruled RULES. Not a keyword match on the jewel text."}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Bonaire?","a":"Dive discipline, not danger. Because Bonaire is 24/7 drive-up shore diving, hold the no-fly 18-24h window and manage repetitive profiles. The on-island hyperbaric chamber next to the Kralendijk hospital is 24-hour and operational (2026).","source":"o2bonaire.com","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Do I have to pay the Bonaire nature fee and what does it cost?","a":"Yes - a mandatory US$40 STINAPA nature tag for all water activities (2026); it funds no-touch/no-anchor enforcement, fish surveys and reef restoration, and also covers Washington Slagbaai NP. Buy it online before you dive.","source":"bonaire.com","si_tag":"diveglobal"},{"q":"When is the best time to dive Bonaire?","a":"Year-round, but December-April is peak (cooler water, best visibility) and April-August brings the calmest seas and superb viz - Bonaire is south of the hurricane belt so there''s no real storm season.","source":"habitatbonaire.com","si_tag":"diveglobal"},{"q":"Which Bonaire dive sites should I not miss?","a":"The Hilma Hooker wreck (30m), 1000 Steps (shallow, snorkel-friendly), Salt Pier (pillar ecosystems - only when no ship is in port) and a Klein Bonaire boat day; most of the ~89 sites are self-guided drive-and-dive off the yellow stones.","source":"scubatravel.co.uk","si_tag":"diveglobal"},{"q":"Is Bonaire a liveaboard destination?","a":"No - Bonaire is the world''s shore/drive-and-dive capital (unlimited-shore packages, drive-thru tank pickup), not a liveaboard base. 