blurb":"an inland blue hole in the Lucayan cave system \"accessible only with authorized dive instructor\" per the Ministry of Tourism","si":["diveglobal","expedition","wildlife"],"wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":26,"tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","source":"https://www.bahamas.com/islands/grand-bahama-island","accessed":"2026-10-02","commission":"entry non-commissionable (curated) - guide or island tour operator sells around it","commission_basis":"2026-10-05 lane label by the jewel''s nature (CC review) - a landmark, park or natural sight - free or a park fee; a guided island tour is the paid route"},{"name":"Owl''s Hole","blurb":"\"Fresh water blue hole hidden in a vast forest of Caribbean pine\", reached by ATV","si":["adventure","wildlife"],"wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":27,"tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","source":"https://www.bahamas.com/islands/grand-bahama-island","accessed":"2026-10-02","commission":"operator (boat, snorkel or dive trip) - activity affiliate where listed","commission_basis":"2026-10-05 lane label by the jewel''s nature (CC review) - reached by boat or water - sold as a boat, snorkel or dive trip by local operators"},{"name":"Picasso''s Gallery","blurb":"\"a dive spot famous for its vibrant coral heads in the shape of a painter''s palette\"","si":["diveglobal","ocean"],"wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":28,"tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","source":"https://www.bahamas.com/experiences/dive-freeport","accessed":"2026-10-02","commission":"venue (retail) - non-commissionable; a guided town or shopping tour sells around it","commission_basis":"2026-10-05 lane label by the jewel''s nature (CC review) - a market, shop or gallery - free to visit; a guided tour is the paid route"},{"name":"Daddy Brown''s Conch and Seafood Stand","blurb":"named by Port Lucaya Marketplace \"for authentic Bahamian Island treats\"","si":["culinary","culture"],"commission":"venue","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":29,"tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","source":"https://www.portlucaya.com/","accessed":"2026-10-02"},{"name":"Sabor Restaurant & Bar","blurb":"the on-site restaurant and bar at Pelican Bay Hotel, Port Lucaya","si":["culinary","romance"],"commission":"venue","wells":["eat","stay"],"draw_rank":30,"tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","source":"https://www.pelicanbayhotel.com/","accessed":"2026-10-02","wells_basis":"full pass 2026-10-05, additive — text"},{"name":"Taino Beach Resort & Clubs","blurb":"a membership resort: \"Unlock the Ultimate Paradise with Taino Beach Resort & Clubs Membership\"; site lists Flamingo Bay Hotel & Marina, watersports, a restaurant and weddings, and Interval International","si":["family","tropical"],"commission":"hotel","wells":["activities","eat","stay"],"draw_rank":32,"tier_absent_reason":"not-established","source":"https://tainobeach.com/","accessed":"2026-10-02","wells_basis":"full pass 2026-10-05, additive — text"},{"name":"Coconut & Fruit Daiquiri Stand","blurb":"\"our famous Coconut & Fruit Daiquiri Stand\" at Port Lucaya Marketplace","si":["culinary","entertainment"],"commission":"venue","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":33,"tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","source":"https://www.portlucaya.com/","accessed":"2026-10-02"}],"faq":[{"q":"What is worth doing in Grand Bahama / Freeport?","a":"Tiger Beach shark liveaboard — multi-day tiger + lemon + hammerhead shark dives.","source":"https://www.liveaboard.com/diving/bahamas/tiger-beach"},{"q":"How do I get to Grand Bahama Island?","a":"By air into Freeport (FPO): the Ministry of Tourism lists American Airlines daily from Miami, Bahamasair from Fort Lauderdale and Raleigh, Sunwing from Toronto and Montreal, and Western Air daily from Nassau and Fort Lauderdale. By sea, Balearia sails Fort Lauderdale to Freeport on Tuesday, Thursday and Saturday; the Bahamas Paradise Cruise service is listed as \"Temporarily Suspended\".","source":"https://www.bahamas.com/getting-here/flying","accessed":"2026-10-02"},{"q":"How do I get from Nassau to Grand Bahama?","a":"The Ministry of Tourism lists Western Air with daily service from Nassau to Freeport. Bahamas Ferries also has a Freeport office (807-8018) and takes reservations on (242) 323-2166 Ext. 250; its homepage did not show a Freeport schedule.","source":"https://www.bahamas.com/getting-here/flying","accessed":"2026-10-02"},{"q":"Can you take a ferry to Grand Bahama?","a":"Yes. The Ministry of Tourism lists \"Balearia: Ft. Lauderdale, FL | Freeport, Grand Bahama | Tu, Th, Sa\". The Bahamas Paradise Cruise service is listed as \"Temporarily Suspended\".","source":"https://www.bahamas.com/getting-here/flying","accessed":"2026-10-02"},{"q":"What is the Grand Bahama airport redevelopment?","a":"The Nassau Guardian reported on June 20, 2025 that the redevelopment \"commenced in March 2024 with demolition of the old terminal\", that the international terminal had been upgraded, and that Dr Kenneth Romer was \"very optimistic that Grand Bahama will see a new airport come 2026.\" No page read on 2026-10-02 confirmed an opening.","source":"https://www.thenassauguardian.com/news/romer-optimistic-that-gb-could-have-new-airport-in-2026/article_58c3a396-cd7c-4aa6-980c-bbc8e731fc1f.html","accessed":"2026-10-02"},{"q":"What is the Grand Bahama Island cruise port?","a":"There are two. Carnival''s Celebration Key, \"at Sharp Rocks, on the eastern coast of Grand Bahama Island\", \"was officially opened and inaugurated on July 19, 2025\". The Port Lucaya Freeport cruise port lies about 20 miles to its west; in February 2024 an $80 million cruise port and water park there was \"slated for completion towards the end of 2026\" (Eyewitness News).","source":"https://www.cruisemapper.com/ports/celebration-key-bahamas-port-2144?tab=news","accessed":"2026-10-02"},{"q":"What are the all-inclusive resorts on Grand Bahama?","a":"Viva Fortuna Beach by Wyndham describes itself as \"the sole all-inclusive resort on the island\", with 274 rooms, three a la carte venues, a buffet and two full-service bars.","source":"https://vivaresortsbywyndham.com/resorts/viva-fortuna-beach-by-wyndham-freeport-grand-bahama/","accessed":"2026-10-02"},{"q":"What can you do on Grand Bahama Island?","a":"The Ministry of Tourism names Lucayan National Park and its underwater caves, Gold Rock Beach, Peterson Cay National Park, the Rand Nature Centre, the Garden of the Groves, Owl''s Hole, Deadman''s Reef for snorkelling, Port Lucaya Marketplace, and West End for \"bonefishing and big game fishing\".","source":"https://www.bahamas.com/islands/grand-bahama-island","accessed":"2026-10-02"},{"q":"What time zone is Grand Bahama in?","a":"\"The Bahamas falls in the Eastern Time Zone, and follows Daylight Saving Time.\"","source":"https://www.bahamas.com/faq","accessed":"2026-10-02"},{"q":"When is Junkanoo in Grand Bahama?","a":"The Ministry of Tourism dates the main parades to Boxing Day, December 26, and New Year''s Day (January 1, 2026 in its December 2025 release), and says Grand Bahama hosts \"their own spectacular versions\". It gives no Grand Bahama venue or time.","source":"https://www.bahamas.com/pressroom/junkanoo-when-a-bahamian-december-beats-loudest","accessed":"2026-10-02"},{"q":"What is there for kids on Grand Bahama Island?","a":"Sanctuary Bay''s Dolphin Encounter is billed \"Great option for all ages!\" ($85 adults, $50 children, excluding VAT), and its Glass Bottom Boat Adventure is \"perfect for all ages\" ($65 adults, $55 children, 1.5 hours).","source":"https://www.unexso.com/","accessed":"2026-10-02"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Grand Bahama & Freeport: Tiger Beach & UNEXSO","meta_description":"Dive Tiger Beach sharks, hand-feed reef sharks at UNEXSO and explore Lucayan caves from Grand Bahama. When to go and how.","slug":"grand-bahama-freeport-bahamas","primary_keyword":"Tiger Beach shark liveaboard","long_tail":["UNEXSO shark dive Freeport","Lucayan National Park Gold Rock Beach","Grand Bahama diving","Freeport Bahamas excursions","Grand Bahama liveaboard"],"jsonl